      "created_at": "2015-06-17T21:14:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><b>Pike Industrial Complex</b></p><p>&nbsp;Here's some pointers on surviving this dangerous place.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul>\n<li>Types of Cards: Rats and Vats</li>\n<li>Number of target cards: 4 rats</li>\n<li>The Vats build up until a vat explosion occurs dealing damage per vat destroyed plus three.</li>\n<li><span>The snowball of the vats is stealthy &amp; deadly. If a regen vat stays out, you may not even care if some cryogenic vats come out... Until an irradiated vat appears. Stuff of nightmares right there.</span></li>\n</ul><ul><li>Dificulty rank - 3 (According to the wiki)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>&nbsp;Villains with this environment</strong></p><ul><li>Thematically Plague Rat works well with this environment&nbsp;<span>His toxic mitigation makes the Pike Industrial vats a warm bath to him, &amp; his many separate instances of damage run away with the damage increase.</span>\n</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Heros with this environment</strong></p><ul><li>\n<b>The Irradiated cyclohexane vat:&nbsp;</b> increases all damage dealt the boost is helpful to all heros, especially those that deal one and those that deal one and one. On the other hand it&nbsp;<span>changes all damage to toxic and this can mess up several heroes. Wraith, Absolute Zero, Ra.&nbsp;</span>\n</li></ul><ul><li>Heroes that reduce environment damage are essential here. (Wraith, Visionary)</li></ul><p>Anything I should add? Tips thoughts? Suggestions? Thanks for the help!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:52.901Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
